{'symbol': 'FE', 'date': '2023-06-21 15:48:00', 'title': 'MARYLAND PUBLIC SERVICE COMMISSION APPROVES POTOMAC EDISON PROPOSAL AIMED AT SAVING CUSTOMERS UP TO $80 MILLION', 'text': "WARRIOR RUN POWER GENERATION CONTRACT TO END SEVEN YEARS EARLY WILLIAMSPORT, MD. , JUNE 21, 2023 /PRNEWSWIRE/ -- THE MARYLAND PUBLIC SERVICE COMMISSION (PSC) HAS APPROVED A PROPOSAL FROM POTOMAC EDISON, A SUBSIDIARY OF FIRSTENERGY (NYSE: FE), TO BUY OUT ITS CONTRACT WITH\xa0AES'S WARRIOR RUN GENERATING STATION APPROXIMATELY SEVEN YEARS EARLY, POTENTIALLY SAVING CUSTOMERS NEARLY $80 MILLION."}